pi.github.com/users/vitrioil/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitrioil/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitrioil/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-04-11T16:22:09Z","updated_at":"2022-04-11T16:22:09Z","body":"I can work on this.\r\n\r\n@albanD I was just checking this. It throws this error:\r\n```bash\r\nterminate called after throwing an instance of 'c10::Error'\r\n  what():  File ./aaa/bbb.pt cannot be opened.\r\n```\r\nFollowed by a huge dump.\r\n\r\nIt comes from [inline_container.cc](https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/3001bda3042eaee01f2e8c4b7b28da74b3566065/caffe2/serialize/inline_container.cc#L341).\r\n\r\nThis change comes from here: #44266\r\n\r\nThis seems to be the desired behaviour to avoid double exception. If I comment this [line](https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/3001bda3042eaee01f2e8c4b7b28da74b3566065/caffe2/serialize/inline_container.cc#L341), it throws this error:\r\n```bash\r\nterminate called after throwing an instance of 'c10::Error'\r\n  what():  [enforce fail at inline_container.cc:423] . PytorchStreamWriter failed writing file data/0: file write failed\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhich is also not meaningful in the context of this issue. Maybe we need to add a parent directory check and inform the user about this by explicitly mentioning that parent directory doesn't exist.\r\n\r\nWould this make sense to do or leave it as it is?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/1095267322/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"vitrioil","id":41074533,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMDc0NTMz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41074533?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitrioil","html_ur